          "number": 9,
          "letter": "I",
          "english": "Of course, finding that balance probably shouldn't be something you have to do by yourself. Research by Erin Kelly, professor of work and organisation studies at MIT, shows companies and managers can play a key role in creating a better environment for workers. For her book Overload: How Good Jobs Went Bad and What to Do about It, she and co-author Phyllis Moen split more than 1,000 employees at a Fortune 500 company into two groups, one that worked under a management redesign and one that continued working within the existing management structure.",
          "chinese": "当然,找到那种平衡可能不应该是你必须独自完成的事情。MIT工作与组织研究教授Erin Kelly的研究表明,公司和管理者可以在为员工创造更好的环境方面发挥关键作用。在她的著作《超载:好工作如何变坏以及该怎么办》中,她和合著者Phyllis Moen将《财富》500强公司的1000多名员工分为两组,一组在管理重新设计下工作,另一组继续在现有管理结构内工作。",
